  "name": "libjpeg",
  "description": "A highly optimized implementation of the Independent JPEG Group's library for image compression and decompression, serving as a critical 3rd-party dependency within the Qt framework. It provides a comprehensive suite of routines for DCT-based image coding, supporting both Huffman and arithmetic entropy encoding across varying bit depths including 8, 12, and 16-bit precision. The codebase incorporates specialized components for color space conversion, quantization, and inverse DCT, featuring performance enhancements likely derived from the libjpeg-turbo project.",
